# Localhost ghost session

The Cursor browser cannot complete Google OAuth on localhost (`origin_mismatch`). Do not try to sign in with the user's Google account.

- Open local Vite with `?ghost=1` (Hub, Notes, or Planner). That sets email `cursor-ghost@localhost` and a default `👻 Cursor` profile (skip with `&noprofile=1`).
- `&fresh=1` wipes leftover `jb_profile` keys and seeds two sample names so the first-launch chooser appears (`?ghost=1&fresh=1`).
- Ghost stays on until `?ghost=0` or **Sair**. It never activates on production hosts.
- Notes and Planner load a canned fixture (lists, a weekend plan, hours). Edits stay in memory and do not hit Drive. Tours are skipped so they do not block clicks.
- Finance, Fit, and Study still have no fixture — do not expect those workbooks to load.
- After `?ghost=1`, exercise the UI as a signed-in user. Do not inject fake greet/`jb_profile` text unless you are testing a failure path.
